  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Would there be a way to implement a system to automatically discard tracking data from trackers and controllers that are in a location that would be impossible to reach when being worn on a human.\nThat way if trackers decide to do a trip around the world you wont end up scrunched up or have your arm suddenly perform inappropriate movements in public.\nTo accommodate for the more flexible and limber users of VRChat I would suggest to bind this feature to a slider that ranges from a strict \"anything outside of sitting/standing/waving/walking\" to a more accommodating \"break dancer/circus performer\" level (and ending at completely disabled) \nWould be great to avoid situations like this: https://twitter.com/RileyDPS/status/1554928133945663488",
